        HelpPage(slug: "arranging", title: "Arranging, aligning, locking and hiding", group: "Objects", summary: "Every object on a layer sits somewhere in a stack: what is drawn later covers what was drawn earlier.  The Modify Arrange commands move objects up and down that stack; the Align panel lines objects up with one another or with the page; locking keeps an object from being changed; hiding takes it off the screen until you ask for it back.",
                 headings: ["Stacking order", "Aligning and distributing", "Locking", "Hiding", "Working with others"],
