        HelpPage(slug: "comments", title: "Comments", group: "Collaboration", summary: "A comment is a note pinned to the drawing: \"make this red\", \"is this the approved logo?\", \"@Priya can you check the kerning here?\".  Comments live in the document, next to the artwork they are about, so a conversation about the star badge happens on the star badge rather than in an email that has to describe where the star badge is.  Anyone who can open the document can read them; commenters, editors and owners can write them; and everyone who is mentioned finds out.  Comments are part of the document and sync like everything else, but they are never part of the artwork: they do not print, and they are left out of exports unless you ask for them.",
                 headings: ["Pins and threads", "Adding a comment", "Editing and deleting your comments", "Mentioning people", "Reactions", "Resolving a thread", "The Comments panel", "Showing and hiding pins", "Being told about comments", "Comments and exports", "Comments on branches", "Who may do what", "Working with others"],
