        HelpPage(slug: "connectors", title: "Connector lines", group: "Drawing", summary: "A connector line links two objects and stays linked: move either object and the line reroutes itself to keep them joined.  Connectors are the quick way to draw call-out lines, organization charts and flowcharts.  A connector is drawn with the current stroke, so its arrowheads, width and dashes come from the Object panel like any other stroke (Stroke attributes).",
