        HelpPage(slug: "creating-text", title: "Creating text", group: "Type", summary: "Every piece of text in a WireTuner document lives in a text block: an object you create with the Text tool and then type into.  A text block behaves like any other object -- you can move it, color it, transform it, stack it on a layer -- and inside it the text has its own world of fonts, paragraphs, tabs and styles.  This page covers the moment of creation: choosing between a block that grows as you type and one with a fixed size, typing the first characters, and what happens to that text when several people are in the document at once.  What you can do with the block afterwards is on Working with text blocks; formatting is on Setting type specifications and the pages that follow it.",
